    "title": "nsacl6",
    "type": "object"
  },
  "description": "The IPv6 access\u2011control rule now called **acl6_rule_10** is applied to interface **eth0** under the ACL identifier **ipv6_acl_01**. It is a **CLASSIC**\u2011type rule with a priority of **5** and is currently **ENABLED**. For IPv6 traffic the rule\u2019s action is **ALLOW**, while the generic ACL action is set to **DENY**. The rule is stateful (**YES**) and is logged (**ENABLED**), with the kernel reporting the rule as **APPLIED**. So far the rule has matched **1\u202f024** packets, has a rate\u2011limit of **1\u202f000** packets per second, and enforces a time\u2011to\u2011live of **64** hops. It is bound to VLAN **100** and VXLAN **5000**, and carries a traffic\u2011direction identifier of **10**.\n\nThe matching criteria are as follows: the source address is **2001:db8::2** (IPv6 flag set to **false**) with an equality operator (**=**) on the source IP, a source MAC of **00:1A:2B:3C:4D:5E** masked by **FF:FF:FF:FF:FF:00**, and a source port condition of **not equal (NEQ)** to **80**. The destination address is the IPv6 value **2001:db8::1**, required to be **not equal (!=)** to that value, and the destination port must equal (**EQ**) **443**. The protocol is **TCP** (protocol number **6**), and the rule does not consider the connection to be established. For DFD processing the hash algorithm **SIP-SPORT-DIP-DPORT** is used with a prefix length of **24**. Additionally, the rule specifies ICMP type **8** and code **3** should be matched when applicable.",
